{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Customer Churn Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook develops a reproducible classification pipeline for identifying\n",
    "telecom customers at risk of leaving. It uses IBM's fictional Telco Customer\n",
    "Churn sample with 7,043 customer records.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business objective:** prioritize customers for retention outreach while\n",
    "detecting as many true churners as reasonably possible.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Load and validate the dataset\n",
    "2. Inspect target balance and data quality\n",
    "3. Split training and test data\n",
    "4. Build a leakage-safe preprocessing pipeline\n",
    "5. Train class-balanced logistic regression\n",
    "6. Evaluate holdout and cross-validated performance\n",
    "7. Interpret the strongest model signals\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n",
    "    f1_score, roc_auc_score\n",
    ")\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score, train_test_split\n",
    "\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "if PROJECT_ROOT.name == \"notebooks\":\n",
    "    PROJECT_ROOT = PROJECT_ROOT.parent\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.churn_pipeline import RANDOM_STATE, build_pipeline, coefficient_table, load_data\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load and validate the data\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Rows: 7,043\n",
      "Input features: 19\n",
      "Churned customers: 1,869 (26.5%)\n",
      "Missing TotalCharges values: 11\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "data_path = PROJECT_ROOT / \"data\" / \"raw\" / \"Telco-Customer-Churn.csv\"\n",
    "X, y, cleaned = load_data(data_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Rows: {len(cleaned):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Input features: {X.shape[1]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Churned customers: {y.sum():,} ({y.mean():.1%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Missing TotalCharges values: {cleaned['TotalCharges'].isna().sum()}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cleaned[[\n",
    "    \"tenure\", \"Contract\", \"InternetService\",\n",
    "    \"MonthlyCharges\", \"TotalCharges\", \"Churn\"\n",
    "]].head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Understand the target\n",
    "\n",
    "Only 26.5% of customers churned, so accuracy alone can be misleading. A model\n",
    "that predicts \"stayed\" for everyone would already be about 73.5% accurate.\n",
    "\n",
    "![Customer churn distribution](../reports/figures/churn_distribution.png)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Split the data before preprocessing\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Training rows: 5,634\n",
      "Test rows: 1,409\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X,\n",
    "    y,\n",
    "    test_size=0.20,\n",
    "    stratify=y,\n",
    "    random_state=RANDOM_STATE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training rows: {len(X_train):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test rows: {len(X_test):,}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Build and train the pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "The pipeline learns imputation, scaling, and encoding values using only the\n",
    "training data. Numeric features use median imputation and standardization.\n",
    "Categorical features use most-frequent imputation and one-hot encoding.\n",
    "Unknown categories are ignored safely during prediction.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = build_pipeline()\n",
    "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "predictions = model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "probabilities = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Evaluate holdout performance\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Accuracy     0.738\n",
      "Precision    0.504\n",
      "Recall       0.783\n",
      "F1           0.614\n",
      "ROC-AUC      0.841\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "holdout_metrics = pd.Series({\n",
    "    \"Accuracy\": accuracy_score(y_test, predictions),\n",
    "    \"Precision\": precision_score(y_test, predictions),\n",
    "    \"Recall\": recall_score(y_test, predictions),\n",
    "    \"F1\": f1_score(y_test, predictions),\n",
    "    \"ROC-AUC\": roc_auc_score(y_test, probabilities),\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(holdout_metrics.round(3).to_string())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The model identified **293 of 374 actual churners** in the test set. Its high\n",
    "recall is useful when missing a churner is more costly than contacting a\n",
    "customer who would have stayed.\n",
    "\n",
    "![Confusion matrix](../reports/figures/confusion_matrix.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "![ROC curve](../reports/figures/roc_curve.png)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Check stability with cross-validation\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Fold ROC-AUC: [0.847 0.825 0.842 0.863 0.853]\n",
      "Mean ROC-AUC: 0.846 \u00b1 0.012\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "cross_validation = StratifiedKFold(\n",
    "    n_splits=5,\n",
    "    shuffle=True,\n",
    "    random_state=RANDOM_STATE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "cv_auc = cross_val_score(\n",
    "    build_pipeline(),\n",
    "    X_train,\n",
    "    y_train,\n",
    "    scoring=\"roc_auc\",\n",
    "    cv=cross_validation,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Fold ROC-AUC:\", cv_auc.round(3))\n",
    "print(f\"Mean ROC-AUC: {cv_auc.mean():.3f} \u00b1 {cv_auc.std():.3f}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Interpret model signals\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "                             feature  coefficient\n",
      "                              tenure       -1.140\n",
      "                   Contract_Two year       -0.783\n",
      "         InternetService_Fiber optic        0.702\n",
      "                      MonthlyCharges       -0.673\n",
      "             Contract_Month-to-month        0.653\n",
      "                 InternetService_DSL       -0.629\n",
      "                        TotalCharges        0.473\n",
      "     TechSupport_No internet service       -0.281\n",
      "DeviceProtection_No internet service       -0.281\n",
      "                  InternetService_No       -0.281\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "top_signals = coefficient_table(model).head(10)\n",
    "print(top_signals[[\"feature\", \"coefficient\"]].round(3).to_string(index=False))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "![Strongest logistic-regression signals](../reports/figures/top_coefficients.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "Longer tenure and two-year contracts are associated with lower predicted churn,\n",
    "while month-to-month contracts and fiber-optic service are associated with\n",
    "higher predicted churn. These are model associations, not proof of causation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "The pipeline achieves a holdout ROC-AUC of 0.841 and detects 78.3% of true\n",
    "churners. Cross-validation results are consistent across folds, suggesting the\n",
    "result is not dependent on one lucky split.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "- The dataset describes a fictional telecom company.\n",
    "- A real deployment needs monitoring, probability calibration, and drift checks.\n",
    "- The classification threshold should be chosen using actual retention costs.\n",
    "- Coefficients describe associations and should not be treated as causal effects.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
